Collapse the card into a status line with the endpoint's own dot

The row no longer opens onto a wall of fields. The card is closed until
asked for: one line carries a dot, the status word, the endpoint and what
it serves, and everything else unfolds behind it. Opening is a button
with aria-expanded, so the state is announced as well as drawn.

The dot is the card's own because nothing else could be. llama.cpp
ignores the credential, so the page's credential dot never lights for
this family, and the page cannot know whether the server behind the route
is up. The probe goes through llm/discoverModels — the one remote call
that reaches the server — and the same call feeds Test connection, so the
dot and the model list can never disagree: green when the endpoint
answered, red with the reason when it did not, grey while the answer is
still in flight. It runs on mount and after every save or reset, with the
value that write left behind.

The dead llm.listModels call the card made for server facts is gone. This
harness exposes only llm/discoverModels, llm/listProviders and
llm/listConfigurableProviders on the remote, so that call could only
throw into a swallowed catch — which is why the context hint never named
the served model. It now does, read from the same probe.

Coverage: test/card.test.mjs renders the browser half in jsdom against
stubbed remotes through the same __ModuleLoader__ seam the page uses,
asserting the closed shape, the dot per answer, the fields the line
reveals, the re-probe a write triggers, and the slot registration.
check:card reads the closed status line before opening the card.